 "excerpts": [
  {
   "at": "docs/programs/certified-federated-reactive-refinement-2026-10-18/03-source-to-model-proof-gates-and-versioned-cursors.md:7",
   "line": "Never identify: (1) source owner's resource revision, (2) owner stream event cursor, (3) A's acceptance transaction/commit id, (4) Fiber value publication sequence, (5) RFCLI QueryStore SnapshotCursor keyed by (source_id,value_digest), or (6) render transaction id. They have different owners and often different order domains. A true SourceBoundary contains B owner-qualified WId/IId/epoch, resource ref, resource version, committed observation metadata and *a stream cursor at the same B snapshot fence*. A separate A AcceptedReceipt binds the exact SourceBoundary and A unit-of-work commit."
  },
  {
   "at": "docs/programs/certified-federated-reactive-refinement-2026-10-18/03-source-to-model-proof-gates-and-versioned-cursors.md:9",
   "line": "An owner may append event 10 to stream for unrelated resource Y while exported X stays revision 2. The naive sourceRevision=eventCursor assertion is false. Comparison of stream cursors is valid only within one declared owner instance/epoch/stream, or under a separately verified cross-epoch resync mapping."
  },
  {
   "at": "docs/programs/certified-federated-reactive-refinement-2026-10-18/03-source-to-model-proof-gates-and-versioned-cursors.md:16",
   "line": "- Keep max source notification cursor h separate from accepted boundary cursor c, per owner stream epoch, and set sourceDirty=(h>c) after accepting an older in-flight snapshot. All other dirty reasons remain independent. On crash reconcile h from retained replay or an authenticated resync fence."
  },
  {
   "at": "docs/programs/certified-federated-reactive-refinement-2026-10-18/03-source-to-model-proof-gates-and-versioned-cursors.md:17",
   "line": "- QueryStore SnapshotCursor is not the federation event cursor and must not share a schema with it."
  },
  {
   "at": "docs/programs/certified-federated-reactive-refinement-2026-10-18/03-source-to-model-proof-gates-and-versioned-cursors.md:33",
   "line": "(a) owner stream cursor advances on unrelated source events, resource revision remains fixed; (b) notification for c=8 arrives while A accepts c=6; outstanding change remains dirty; (c) storage crash at every journal step; (d) A accepts an old authentic snapshot, never claims B latest; (e) lost final event forces unknown without replay/fence; (f) peer instance/epoch mismatch and revocation; (g) pin changes during graph render; (h) observer sees status/provenance changes despite equal payload; (i) tokenized source identity and typed permission preserving replay; (j) finite LTS simulation rejects an unmatched visible error and rejects τ mislabeled when observer-visible state changes."
  },
  {
   "at": "docs/programs/certified-federated-reactive-refinement-2026-10-18/README.md:22",
   "line": "ResourceKey = (owner WId, backend IId, resource kind/name, definition revision, output port, type/schema digest, export contract revision)."
  },
  {
   "at": "docs/programs/certified-federated-reactive-refinement-2026-10-18/README.md:25",
   "line": "Do not reuse a render transaction id as the source revision; do not use an alias as owner identity; no implicit 'latest' guarantee."
  },
  {
   "at": "docs/programs/certified-federated-reactive-refinement-2026-10-18/README.md:28",
   "line": "1. Resolve explicit alias through B public API; compare expected WId/IId and export contract; check B authorizes this particular read and A independently authorizes admission."
  },
  {
   "at": "docs/programs/certified-federated-reactive-refinement-2026-10-18/02-concrete-contract-and-verification-gates.md:20",
   "line": "The fields \\`sourceResourceRevision\\`, \\`sourceStreamFence\\`, \\`acceptedStreamCursor\\`, \\`consumerAcceptanceCommit\\` and \\`publishTransaction\\` MUST be separately typed. In particular, an unrelated journal event advances stream cursor without changing resource revision. A source epoch change makes old/new cursors incomparable. A render can publish an earlier accepted pin after a later accept provided the earlier pin is visible and policy permits it; it must never retag F(old) as F(new)."
  },
